 "1759433016208x997641308276785200": "Simple Dropdown Bubble Mobile",
 "_comment": "Bubble marketplace plugin ID -> display name. IDs are marketplace-global (same ID = same plugin in every app), so this cache is reusable across projects. Value forms: \"Name\" = known listed plugin; null = looked up but unavailable (delisted, name unknown); {\"name\": ..., \"author\": ..., \"delisted\": true} = object form; author is the seller display name. Resolve new IDs via the PUBLIC Data API: https://bubble.io/api/1.1/obj/plugin/<id> (name_text, owner_user, official_badge_boolean) -> /obj/user/<owner_user> (organization_custom_organization) -> /obj/organization/<org> (name_text = author). Works even when the marketplace page renders only the generic shell. Built-in short-name plugins (chartjs, apiconnector2, ...) are authored by Bubble. Keys starting with '_' are ignored."
